From: finalpantasy <finalpantasy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:02:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/34] Windows timer resolution, inline quiet SSE path

- platform_win: timeBeginPeriod(1) and opt out of hidden-window timer
  throttling, so timed waits stop rounding up to the 15.6 ms tick.
- kernel32 Sleep goes through platform::SleepUntilNs on Windows.
- sse_quiet.h: the no-MXCSR-switch fast path for Arith, Sqrt and
  MinMax is inline in generated code; sse.cpp keeps the full paths.
- sse.cpp builds without auto-vectorization (it made Windows x64
  prologues save XMM6-15).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
